2026-08-25T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-1139) 'Four rig conventions are measured off the geometry, and a mismatch stops the render.
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD1139  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-1139) 'Three defects came from assuming a convention, each producing a result that looked correct.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD1139  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-1139) 'Read `SKILL.md` for the order of the checks and the traps.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD1139  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-1139) 'Scale, up, forward and handedness are measured
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD1139  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-1139) '`check_conventions.py` measures four properties off the geometry and refuses on a mismatch. `render_grid.py` runs it before rendering a frame, and reports which checks could not run rather than passing over them. `SKILL.md` gives the order and the traps.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD1139  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-1139) 'Forward is the chest, the normal to the shoulder line. Gaze and feet are secondary: on the hv_1 fit the chest and gaze agree to 2.8 degrees while the feet sit 55.3 degrees away, so a stance is not a defect.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD1139  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-1139) 'Handedness takes three witnesses. The `.R` against `.L` split cannot catch a mirror alone, since `right` comes from the chest and the chest mirrors with the body. Signed mesh volume and basis determinants do.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD1139  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-1139) 'RFD66606-1134 records the fits these were written against. RFD66606-1137 encodes the render order they guard.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD1139  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-1139) 'The three defects
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1139  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-1139) 'The 2D fit projected components 0 and 1 while the rig is Z-up, so the solver rotated every body ninety degrees and reported 0.022% of stature. `stature` measured the body's depth for the same reason, normalising by 0.434 where 1.660 belonged. The camera grid placed cameras at world azimuth while its phrases claim a subject's front, so 96 frames labelled "front view" were profiles.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1139  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-1139) 'The problem
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1139  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-1139) 'None raised anything. A left-right swap is worse: it reprojects onto the same pixels, reports the same residual and passes the referee, because both measure reprojection.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1139  1 LINE
 Text:Written
